## What's changed?

Fixing an edge case of Java parsing. Namely when a single-line empty comment is at the end of the file and there's no newline after that.
```
class A {
}
//
```

## What's your motivation?

Feedback from one of the OpenRewrite users.

One-time follow up to #269 , which gets all files in codebase aligned with the newly-defined import rules.

These imports were auto-adjusted after running this from the CLI: `yarn prettier --write --ignore-unknown .`

Going forward, that prettier command will be automatically run on staged files during each commit.

In addition to blind formatting, this also sneaks in a couple minor fixes:
* Created a new `init.ts` files to handle environment configuration and module aliasing. This file imports `dotenv` and `module-alias`, sets up aliases for `@backend` and `@core`, and configures environment variables.
* Fixes TS issues in `declaration.d.ts`, which were causing prettier command to fail

Finally, it omits the default ordering for a few files by using comments:

```
//init.ts

// sort-imports-ignore
import dotenv from "dotenv";
import moduleAlias from "module-alias";
import path from "path";
moduleAlias.addAliases({
  "@backend": `${__dirname}`,
  "@core": `${path.resolve(__dirname, "../../core/src")}`,
});
// eslint-disable-next-line prettier/prettier
import { Logger } from "@core/logger/winston.logger";
```
> notice how `// eslint-disable-next-line prettier/prettier` is placed _below_ the relevant line
